  "summary": "PostgreSQL to_char heap buffer overflow executes arbitrary code",
  "details": "Heap buffer overflow in PostgreSQL to_char(timestamptz) allows the party choosing the timezone to execute arbitrary code as the operating system user running the database, via a long POSIX timezone abbreviation.  Versions before PostgreSQL 18.6, 17.11, 16.15, 15.19, and 14.24 are affected.",
